# 🚀 Day 15 - Set Matrix Zeroes

## 📌 Problem

LeetCode #73 - Set Matrix Zeroes

Given an m x n matrix, if an element is 0,
set its entire row and column to 0.

The matrix must be modified in-place.

---

## 🏷️ Difficulty

Medium

---

## 📚 Topics

- Arrays
- Matrix
- In-Place Manipulation

---

## 💡 Approach

Use the first row and first column as markers.

Maintain two flags:

- row0 → whether the first row contains 0
- col0 → whether the first column contains 0

For every zero in the inner matrix:

- Mark its row using matrix[i][0]
- Mark its column using matrix[0][j]

Then use those markers to set the required
cells to zero.

Finally, handle the first row and first column.

---

## 🧪 Example

Input:

[
 [1,1,1],
 [1,0,1],
 [1,1,1]
]

Output:

[
 [1,0,1],
 [0,0,0],
 [1,0,1]
]

---

## ⚡ Complexity

Time Complexity: O(m × n)

Space Complexity: O(1)

---

## 🧠 Key Learning

The first row and first column can be reused
as storage for row and column information.

Important pattern:

First Row + First Column = Markers

---

## 🎯 Pattern

Matrix Traversal
+
In-Place Marking
+
Constant Space

---

## ✅ Status

Accepted ✔️

##Code
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

using namespace std;

class Solution {
public:
    void setZeroes(vector<vector<int>>& matrix) {

        int m = matrix.size();
        int n = matrix[0].size();

        bool row0 = false;
        bool col0 = false;

        // Check first column
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            if (matrix[i][0] == 0)
                col0 = true;
        }

        // Check first row
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            if (matrix[0][j] == 0)
                row0 = true;
        }

        // Mark rows and columns
        for (int i = 1; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {

                if (matrix[i][j] == 0) {
                    matrix[i][0] = 0;
                    matrix[0][j] = 0;
                }
            }
        }

        // Apply markers
        for (int i = 1; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {

                if (matrix[i][0] == 0 ||
                    matrix[0][j] == 0) {

                    matrix[i][j] = 0;
                }
            }
        }

        // First row
        if (row0) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
                matrix[0][j] = 0;
        }

        // First column
        if (col0) {
            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)
                matrix[i][0] = 0;
        }
    }
};

int main() {

    Solution obj;

    vector<vector<int>> matrix = {
        {1, 1, 1},
        {1, 0, 1},
        {1, 1, 1}
    };

    obj.setZeroes(matrix);

    cout << "Result Matrix:\n";

    for (auto& row : matrix) {
        for (int x : row) {
            cout << x << " ";
        }
        cout << endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
